## How to Run & Test

### Development (Expo Go)
```bash
cd d:\Clients\RemindMe
npx expo start
```
Scan the QR code with **Expo Go** on your Android phone.

> [!NOTE]
> Custom alarm sounds won't work in Expo Go — they require a dev build. All other features work in Expo Go.

### Dev Build (full features including alarm sound)
```bash
npx expo run:android
```

---

## How to Build APK

```bash
# 1. Install EAS CLI (one-time)
npm install -g eas-cli

# 2. Login to your Expo account
eas login

# 3. Build APK
eas build -p android --profile preview

# 4. Download the .apk from the URL provided by EAS
```

Expected APK size: **~15-20 MB**

> [!TIP]
> The `preview` profile in [eas.json](file:///d:/Clients/RemindMe/eas.json) is configured to output `.apk` (not `.aab`), so you can directly install it on any Android device without the Play Store.
